fcitx5-vanh (6.0.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Surrounding text through GNOME Shell: pace edits and wait for the app to
    show the text an edit deletes, so fast typing no longer garbles words
    ("được" became "đươcợc").
  * Switch a field to the uinput server when the app drops deletions (Apple
    Notes on the web, Messenger on facebook.com).
  * Revert key: turns the last word to its other reading (English <->
    Vietnamese); it waits for its modifiers to go up.
  * Enter restores the word like a word break, sent through the uinput server.
  * English restore: better context for developer text and for same-looking
    words after a clearly Vietnamese word.
  * English restore keeps a word the Telex undo made ("inss" stays "ins"),
    so Enter in the Chromium address bar opens the suggested site.
  * Harden the IPC between the addon and the uinput server.
  * New tray icons: a V badge, a grey E badge and a smiley.

 -- congmnguyen <kv8haiquan@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 22:58:38 +0700

fcitx5-vanh (6.0.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename the package, addon, input method, server and data paths from lotus
    to vanh; migrate the old user configuration and service enablement.
  * Add detection of the address bar in Chromium-based browsers on X11.
  * Fix bug w2u in surrounding text mode
  * Fix bug cannot restore invalid word on uinput mode

